@AnHebrewChild  The exact scenario Ed is describing just started happening today, which essentially is that hyperscalers are functionally trapped in a financial circle jerk (as Jon put it) of their own making. 
If Amazon, Google, or Microsoft cut their CapEx, they starve the AI labs like Anthropic and Open AI. If the labs starve, they can't pay their massive, multi-billion-dollar cloud bills back to Amazon, Google, and Microsoft. If the labs stop paying their cloud bills, the hyperscalers' core cloud revenue growth—the very engine driving their stock prices crashes. It really is a giant circle jerk that can't last, especially under high inflation and borrowing costs. Because these hyperscalers are so large, they can bring down the entire financial market if their share prices fall enough. When you combine that with today's news that Anthropic looks like it won't even get an A rating, and basically, it's looking like the beginning of the bust. 
Sorry for the long diatribe, it's late. Hope that helps.

