@amonkeysden If you actually read the S1 it shows a 2.6 Billion net income for H1 2026, with a 10% margin. This is an adjusted figure given the unique nature of the options disbursements for Anthropic, but that's hardly "fake accounting" 

Now 2.6B isn't a lot given the target market cap but it shows they can actually sell model intelligence to customers at a profit, which is one of the 2 lynchpins that decide if this is a bubble or not (the 2nd being that neocloud providers can actually sell inference at a profit, which is the stronger bubble argument). 

Given Anthropic is managing to grow their revenue and scale at a truly absurd rate and has managed to turn itself profitable on a unit margin basis, it seems reasonable that they'd be able to continue to scale that up especially seeing how model capabilities are continuing to accelerate rather than plateau (Here's where Ed is MOST wrong)

@BurningTNT please point out the things that I stated that you think "lack actual evidence" and I will be happy to provide you with said evidence.

On the peak AI point - I'm not padding, it actually makes each of his incorrect claims all the more egregious because time would've passed where he would've seen subsequent frontier models released... which are measurably superior in both capabilities and efficiencies to their predecessors (there's no shorting of standardized model benchmarking metrics that categorically prove this to be true)... so not acknowledging that I think is insane.

Also goes to your "subjective" argument about the claim that AI peaking, because not only are there empirical data points that prove the frontier keeps getting pushed by each new model release. But also many of these claims were made well prior to the agentic AI revolution which is the reason why memory needs, token usage, and frontier lab revenues have exploded in the last year as the practical use cases (and value generation) for end consumers has exploded. First beginning with commercial applications and now expanding into consumer with Grok Bot, Muse, and Dots.

